        "description": "Mid-cruise refinement."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 160,
        "type": "tcm",
        "label": "TCM-3",
        "description": "Approach trim toward Meridiani Planum target ellipse."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 195,
        "type": "tcm",
        "label": "TCM-4 — final pre-EDL",
        "description": "Final trim before the atmospheric entry interface."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 202,
        "type": "arrival",
        "label": "Mars approach + cruise-stage separation",
        "description": "2004-01-25. Cruise stage jettisoned; backshell + heat shield + lander entered the atmosphere at 5.5 km/s."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 202.005,
        "type": "edl_or_oi",
        "label": "Mars EDL — airbag landing in Meridiani Planum",
        "description": "Bounced 26 times across the hematite-rich plains of Meridiani Planum and rolled into a 22-m diameter crater — Eagle Crater — by sheer luck. The first close-up images showed bedrock exposing in the crater walls, geology a rover could read without driving anywhere. Found jarosite and \"blueberry\" hematite concretions, the strongest mineral evidence to that point of standing liquid water on early Mars. Traversed 45.16 km over 14+ years — a record until Perseverance passed it in October 2026. Final transmission 2018-06-10 during a planet-wide dust storm; NASA declared end-of-mission 2019-02-13."
      }
